  {
   "id": 520985,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "In vertebrates, cartilage is found in fetal bones, ears, and intervertebral discs, whereas bone is found in the skeleton. What are the similarities between cartilage and bone?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1018265,
     "content_html": "Both are types of connective tissue in the body and cells of both are known as chondrocytes."
    },
    {
     "id": 1018266,
     "content_html": "Both are types of connective tissue in the body and have non-vascular organic matrix material that provides strength and flexibility."
    },
    {
     "id": 1018267,
     "content_html": "Both are types of connective tissue in the body and have organic matrix material that provides strength and flexibility."
    },
    {
     "id": 1018268,
     "content_html": "Both consist of bone marrow and have organic matrix material that provides strength and flexibility."
    }
   ],
